{
  "info": {
    "name": "Hospigo 7c doctor profile",
    "description": "Step 7c (API): doctor profile details (printed name, qualifications, speciality, registration number) and the copy a completed prescription keeps. BEFORE RUNNING: (1) npm run prisma:migrate -w @hospigo/api  (2) re-run the dev seed so the roles get the new permissions: NODE_ENV=development npm run prisma:seed -w @hospigo/api  (3) restart the API on port 3000. Select the Hospigo Local environment (staffPassword and superadminPassword), then Run collection. It uses Doctor North 3, puts that profile back as it was, and makes ONE paid visit and one completed prescription to prove the copy never changes. About 4 logins count against the login IP limit (20 per minute).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 Setup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 Login Doctor North 3",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/hospital/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "hospital",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"accessCode\":\"demo-north-main\",\"email\":\"{{doctorEmail}}\",\"password\":\"{{staffPassword}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('select the Hospigo Local environment: staffPassword and superadminPassword must be set', () => { pm.expect(pm.variables.get('staffPassword'), 'staffPassword').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty; pm.expect(pm.variables.get('superadminPassword'), 'superadminPassword').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty; });",
                  "pm.test('login 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('has a token', () => pm.expect(j.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('dDoc', j.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
